  <prompt>Owner UAT round 6 (2026-10-06), items 1-3. Record: `notes/042-uat-round6-2026-10-06.md`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9).</role>

  <goal>The create form reads as its own small form: a title, the type pills that choose what is created, the type's fields, and Cancel / Create in the standard positions.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Owner (round 6)**: (1) in "+ New" mode, clicking another type pill switches the create form to that type
        (Matter → Project shows the Project fields); the user leaves the form with **Cancel**; (2) a header
        **"Create New Record"** above the type pills while the form is open; (3) **Create** on the right, **Cancel** on
        the left — like the other forms (e.g. the Save tab's Cancel left / Save right).
      - **Today** (tasks 099/100): "+ New" shows only the pills + `CreateRecordForm` (per-type fields; required
        markers; Assigned To prefill via `useCreateRecordFormData`). Read `notes/099-save-tab-round5.md` and
        `notes/100-create-record-fields.md` first.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 1">Switching the pill while the form is open keeps the form open and shows the new type's fields. Values that exist on both types (Name, Description, Assigned To) carry over; type-only values (Matter Type, Practice Area, Project Type) do not. The type's required fields and reference lists follow the new type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner items 1, 3">The only way out of the form, other than a successful create, is Cancel. Cancel restores the view the user had before "+ New" (task 099 behaviour).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 2">A heading "Create New Record" sits above the type pills only while the create form is open (semantic heading, not just bold text).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 3">Button row: Cancel left-aligned (secondary), Create right-aligned (primary), matching the Save tab's footer pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 / ADR-021">Same in both hosts; Fluent v9 tokens; fits at 320 px; focus stays sensible when the type switches (it stays on the pill).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Update the tests that pin the form; new suites are REPORTED to the main session for `ci-gated-suites.txt`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">No BFF change; no field added or removed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">With the form open on Matter, clicking Project shows the Project fields with Name/Description/Assigned To carried over and no Matter Type / Practice Area; Create follows Project's required fields.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Create New Record" heading is present only while the form is open.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cancel is left, Create is right; Cancel restores the pre-"+ New" view; a successful create behaves as in task 099/100.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: jest (all suites) green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after deploy): as above. If unavailable, leave open.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the round-6 note, the 099/100 notes, `CreateRecordForm.tsx`, `RelatedToPicker.tsx`.</step>
    <step>Title, type switch, button row; tests.</step>
    <step>Gates; `notes/101-create-form-round6.md`; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>`CreateRecordForm` and the picker's create mode exist (tasks 099/100).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — layout and state changes in the existing form; nothing new.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner UAT round 6 items 1-3: the type cannot be changed mid-form and the buttons are not where the other forms put them.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Create form round 6">
      <steps>
        <step>"+ New" → "Create New Record" above the pills; Matter fields; click Project → Project fields, Name kept.</step>
        <step>Cancel (left) returns to the search view; Create (right) creates.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

